{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on dd4e6dd1 for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\n1. SQLite keys. Key `inbox`, `source_order` and `observed` by\n(scope, genesis). Write no migration. Format word 2 covers the\nschema, and old-format rooms retire at the cutover (c0a795e7).\n\n2. Platform origin algorithms. Keep one method for each question.\nDo not split a method, and do not add a second input family. The\nplatform takes the admitted origin: each row has the body, the\nlabel and `sequence: CheckedSequence | null`. That is the\n`SourceCopy` shape that `admittedOrigin` returns. Define the type\nin derive beside `Fetched`. A `Fetched` is the case with a\nsequence. The calls at delivery.ts:204 and :216 and at\noperations.ts:414 and :415 pass `admittedOrigin(read.origin ?? [],\ncap)`. Inside each algorithm:\n\na. The subject row needs a genuine sequence. So does every row\nwhose own kind the algorithm reads. The kind comes from\n`sequence.kind`. The match is the three-argument `isEntryOf`. A\nfirst entry proves its own sequence, so the subject always\nqualifies.\n\nb. A row with no sequence serves in one role only: the creator\nentry that an admitted first entry names as `source`. The algorithm\nchecks `isEntryBodyOf(row.entry, born.source)` and\n`same(seed.creator, born.source.at)`. It takes the creator's kind\nfrom the `sourceKind` of that admitted first entry. Ruling b02334db\nmakes the recorded kind the authority. No field type, label, pin or\ncaller supplies a kind.\n\nc. The caller passes `directory` and `destination` as full\nreferences from its own fixed places. The `same(...)` comparisons\nagainst them stay. They tie the creator's address to a reference\nthat the caller holds. The tests `directory.kind === \"directory\"`\nand `destination.kind === \"destination\"` go, because the place\nfixes the kind.\n\nd. The nine-row incident origin holds each parent birth in its\nrows. Every row there gets a sequence, and case b covers only the\nroot creator.\n\ne. `sourced` states a native name from its own first entry and the\nretained creator copy under rule b. `genuineCopies` drops the\ncreator copy today, so `nameUnder` gets the admitted copies\ninstead.\n\nIf one algorithm reads a kind that rules a to d do not give, name\nthe line and ask. Do not add a remote read.\n\n3. Recorded position. The position is enough for all three: the\n`isClaims` membership, the directory, membership and rules of the\nsession-reference reply, and the `repositorySessionMembership`\nreference. Each old check read a kind that the sender wrote in the\nreference, so it proved no more than the position does. One\ncondition holds. Each reader that later reads one of those\nsequences compares `sequence.kind` of the admitted birth with the\nkind of the place, and treats a mismatch as a failed read. Name in\nthe review request any use that only compares or forwards the\nreference and never reads the sequence.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}